// ANS - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// ANS is the ANSI X3.68-1976 record format, and the entire
// specification is one rule: every record is exactly as wide as
// the first, records end with a form feed, and so does the file.
//
// There is no header, no metadata and no version field, which makes
// it the shortest of the formats here at eighty-one bytes and also
// the only one whose payload is entirely text.
//
// Hello World! is the record, left-justified and padded to eighty
// characters, which is what the format requires.
//
// ans: 81 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21 20 20 20 20 |Hello World!    |   <- 0000
// 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 |                |   <- 0010
// 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 |                |   <- 0020
// 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 |                |   <- 0030
// 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 |                |   <- 0040
// 0C                                              |.|   <- 0050
